[[File:Bronze axe detail.png|left|130px]]
The '''bronze axe''' is the weakest [[axe]] in ''[[Old School RuneScape]]''. It can be wielded for combat, or used to cut trees in [[Woodcutting]]. It requires an [[Attack]] level of 1 to be equipped, and a Woodcutting level of 1 to be used.

Players can make a bronze axe with the [[Smithing]] skill at level 1 using one [[bronze bar]], giving the player 12.5 Smithing [[experience]]. Players can take one for free from [[logs (bronze axe)|logs]] found at various locations, such as at the chicken farm by the [[Lumbridge cow field]], or [[Fred the Farmer]]'s house. One can also be obtained by talking to the [[Woodsman tutor]].

Various activities require the use of an any axe, such as chopping Kraken tentacles on the [[Fishing Trawler]], defeating the [[Growthling|growthlings]] during the [[Bryophyta]] boss fight, or cutting [[bruma roots]] to fight [[Wintertodt]]. A bronze axe is available to the player from the nearby environment in these activities: on the Fishing Trawler from a crate marked [[Axes (Fishing Trawler)|axes]], at Bryophyta from a pile of [[Logs (bronze axe)|logs]], and at Wintertodt from a [[Crate (Wintertodt)#Axes|crate]].

